From 4d36db64944c89533b770b708d6f4805bb51292d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:32:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution settings: finite elements by kernels on the host
 with --execution cpu

With `--execution cpu`, the gradients, the inner forces and the tangent
operator are computed by kernels on the host by default: on the beam of the
prototype (111 843 unknowns, 10 steps, 8 processes), 12.4 s instead of
16.5 s element by element. This default is optional: at the first setup,
all the processes replace it by the computations element by element if the
behaviour integrators do not support the kernels (for instance elements of
different geometries in a material), instead of failing; a parameter given
to the problem is never replaced. With PETSc, which supports neither, the
behaviours are integrated point by point and the finite elements computed
element by element by default.

ExecutionSettingsTest: the finite elements computed by kernels with
`--execution cpu`, and a square made of a quadrangle and two triangles
(mesh square-quadrangle-triangles.mesh) computed element by element; without
the replacement, the resolution fails (mutation detected). CPU suite
196/196, GPU variants 20/20.
